<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

	<!--
		The brood's egg spew (Phase 5, 2026-09-20). Odyssey's own EggSpew ability, cloned so
		the sac it throws holds a VFEI2 swarmling instead of Odyssey's vanilla larva. The
		clone is what keeps vanilla Odyssey untouched: patching EggSpew or EggSac instead
		would change every vanilla egg sac in the game.

		The chain, and the one link of it that is ours:
		  - this ability launches PMM_Proj_EggSac and nothing else,
		  - PMM_Proj_EggSac is OUR Projectile_EggSac: it spawns PMM_EggSac and copies the
		    queen's brood order onto it,
		  - Projectile_SpawnsThing.Impact gives that sac the LAUNCHER's faction
		    (`thing.SetFaction(base.Launcher.Faction)`), and the sac's spawn comp then spawns
		    the pawn with the sac's faction - so a queen's brood belongs to her faction, in
		    her village, and our code never has to decide it.

		The ability itself is a player's button: nothing casts it on its own. `aiCanUse` is
		false, and the auto-cast comp that used to sit on her race was deleted on 2026-09-26
		(HANDOFF §5.11).

		`gizmoClass` is ours. Command_Ability_EggSpew turns this button into the brood picker as
		well: press it, choose which daughter she lays, then choose the ground. It replaced the
		comp's own picker gizmo, which is deleted, so she has one button where she used to have
		two.

		Two more changes the same day, both the user's call, and together they left this a plain
		sac throw: the cooldown went to fifteen days, and the acid spray half is gone - nothing
		burns, nothing is slimed, and no terrain is laid. See the notes beside the cooldown, the
		range and the comps below.
		See Defs/ThingDefs/Things_EggSpew.xml for the two ThingDefs.

		Odyssey-gated, like the queen herself: the sounds, the spray effecter and the
		sludge projectile it references are all Odyssey content.
	-->
	<AbilityDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
		<defName>PMM_Ability_EggSpew</defName>
		<label>egg spew</label>
		<description>Lay an egg sac on the ground. Break the sac to release the brood inside.</description>
		<iconPath>UI/Icons/Abilities/PMM_EggSpew</iconPath>
		<!-- 15 days (user's call 2026-09-26). One sac per 15 days is the whole throttle on abaddon
		     numbers: 15 x 60000 ticks. It used to be 5000, about two hours. -->
		<cooldownTicksRange>900000</cooldownTicksRange>
		<!-- Player-only button (user's call 2026-09-26). Nothing may cast this on its own: the
		     race's auto-cast comp is gone (§5.11), and this closes the generic AI path too.
		     `displayGizmoWhileUndrafted` keeps it on the player's own queen. -->
		<aiCanUse>false</aiCanUse>
		<displayOrder>300</displayOrder>
		<displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>true</displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>
		<disableGizmoWhileUndrafted>false</disableGizmoWhileUndrafted>
		<!-- The button is also the brood picker (user's call 2026-09-26): our command asks for the
		     caste first, then hands over to vanilla's targeting (see EggSpewAbility.cs).
		     AbilityDef.gizmoClass is vanilla's own hook for this - Command_AbilitySpeech uses it
		     the same way - so she has one button where she used to have two. -->
		<gizmoClass>PMM_Insects.Command_Ability_EggSpew</gizmoClass>
		<warmupStartSound>AcidSpray_Warmup</warmupStartSound>
		<verbProperties>
			<verbClass>Verb_CastAbility</verbClass>
			<!-- 1.9 cells: the ring around her and nothing further (user's call 2026-09-26). Was
			     14.9, a throwing range, back when the acid spray flew with the sac. -->
			<range>1.9</range>
			<warmupTime>0.25</warmupTime>
			<soundCast>AcidSpray_Resolve</soundCast>
			<targetParams>
				<canTargetLocations>true</canTargetLocations>
			</targetParams>
		</verbProperties>
		<comps>
			<!-- The brood, and the only half left: ours instead of Odyssey's Proj_EggSac. The acid
			     spray comp that sat above it was deleted on 2026-09-26. -->
			<li Class="CompProperties_AbilityLaunchProjectile">
				<projectileDef>PMM_Proj_EggSac</projectileDef>
			</li>
		</comps>
	</AbilityDef>

</Defs>
